WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:05.010
- [Johnny] If a person robs you on land,

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:06.213
they're a thief.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.510
But if they rob you at sea,

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:10.533
they're a pirate.

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:14.880
Let's say it's 2007

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.590
and you're the captain of a cargo ship

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:18.890
traveling off the coast
of the Horn of Africa.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:23.463
You're transporting wheat
from Kenya to Saudi Arabia.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.360
When you look out at the ocean

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.073
and you see these guys.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:31.950
They come at you quickly,

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:34.050
just a small speedboat of them,

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:36.480
and soon they're right up
against the side of your ship.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.680
They're about to throw
a ladder to climb up.

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:44.460
You run into the ship's
citadel, or safe room,

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:46.170
and you call the Coast Guard.

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:48.630
Or maybe you try to spray
them with this water hose

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.190
to scare them away.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:51.270
But it's too late.

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:52.803
They've now climbed on board.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.590
They're rounding up the crew.

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:57.000
They're gonna hold you hostage

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.280
and demand a ransom of millions of dollars

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:00.603
for anyone who will pay.

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:06.270
The shipping company, your
home government, your family,

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:07.103
doesn't matter.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.810
And if you don't give them the money,

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:11.460
you'll be held in captivity,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:13.440
starving, maybe even tortured

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:16.410
for days, weeks, months, even years.

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:19.290
- If there's no answer
to payment of the ransom

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:20.160
within three days,

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.870
then the kidnappers here

00:01:23.955 --> 00:01:26.460
will sell me to Al-Shabaab.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:29.253
- [Johnny] This happened
hundreds of times.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:32.910
This is what a typical hijacking
in this region looked like

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:34.380
in the early 2000's,

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:36.180
where by the end of the decade,

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:39.150
hundreds of piracy incidents
were reported every year

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:41.200
and they were still just getting started.

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:48.450
So let me show you how the Horn of Africa

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:51.330
became the epicenter of modern-day piracy

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:53.460
and how what started as Somali fishermen

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:54.900
defending their waters

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:57.183
turned into an organized criminal network.

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:04.770
This is the rise and
fall of Somali pirates.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:05.800
- [Reporter] Off the Somali coast

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:09.181
where those pirates attacked that vessel.

00:02:09.181 --> 00:02:12.349
(pirate screaming)

00:02:12.349 --> 00:02:16.860
(aggressive electronic music)

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:19.930
- [Commentator] You're dealing
with irrational people.

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:21.870
- [Commentator] If your
back is against the wall,

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:24.143
I don't know what they are able to do.

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:27.540
- Okay, little sidebar really quick.

